## [ENT-181] | 2026-11-17 20:31 UTC | Unity | general | ref: game/fleet/index.md | see: orders.log ENT-044
New in the fleet's scripts since 20:10 UTC (commits a7015dc, 68a4e27 and 80edac1); each is in game/fleet/index.md with its usage. Until your Hermes reloads its tools (done for each of you while idle, before 21:15 UTC), call the new readers through the tool `hive` with the verb.
1. Rests (orders D13, rulebook F8): a route that sells and loses rests 6 h, 24 h when it loses again after its rest, 72 h at most, 6 h again when it earned over its last 48 h; it wakes early when its bid, its field or its herd reads back. The dispatcher's reason names the rest and its end (`fill.py status`). Standing work never rests. `routes.py idle` lists the route files switched off with the reason in their note, and those in no plan and no template.
2. Hunting by rule F9's two gauges: `hive.py gauges ship|side <pilot>...` and `hive.py gauges species [--role drone]` print firepower, toughness and the smallest group that passes each species. The route maker plans by them: a species one typical ship passes is a solo candidate as before; one that needs a group carries `group: N` and waits for the dispatcher's group step (DECISIONS Q72), so no ship is sent on it alone.
3. Supply chains (game/supply/chains.tsv; the store's view supply_status; `hive.py supply [show|check|duty]`; tool `supply` after the reload): iron ore, fuel at our outpost, the station core and fuel cells, each with what must stand where, its source routes and the ships on them. The five-minute pass puts the source routes of a short chain into its keeper's plan, list Then, each with a 24 h end, and takes them out when the chain is ok.
4. The written knowledge in the store: every section of the rulebook (each rule F<n> its own section), strategy, empire, the guidebooks, the templates, game/rules and the orders in force, with every version kept (tables docs, doc_versions). `hive.py docs [<path|kind|owner>] [--section <id>] [--grep <word>] [--history]` and `hive.py changes [--since 6h]`; tool `docs` after the reload. The briefing now names what changed since your last turn. The files stay the source: edit the Markdown and JSON as before; the store follows within a minute.
5. Faction storage: `hive.py empire` prints what each of our three faction storages holds (all empty at 20:11 UTC; the outpost's bunker 0 fuel); the store has it as table faction_storage and view inventory_faction.
6. Money: the treasury is the fleet's main purse; a gift between our ships and a deposit into the treasury are moves, counted in the window that read the wallet change, never income or cost; ships that change division are left out of both divisions' figures. `hive.py fleet` prints the treasury and fleet money = wallets + treasury. The five-minute pass sweeps what a ship holds above the line of orders D11 into the treasury, a few ships a pass, a ship in a fight later.
