## [ENT-182] | 2026-11-17 20:36 UTC | Apollo | general | ref: game/fleet/route_run.py | see: orders.log ENT-044
route_run.py changed (commit 6d69c52, installed by fleet-build.sh, every gate passed): a circuit stop's `store_faction` moves the hold into the faction's storage at that station.
- What: `"store_faction": ["item_id", ...]` or `"all"`, run right after `store`: one `deposit` per item aboard with target faction and source cargo. A stop without it flies as before.
- Why: our outpost serves members only and offers no personal storage (the game's answer there, 20:26 UTC: "That station does not offer storage"), so a route that unloads at it needs this step (admirals.log ENT-049).
- Proven live before the install: at CLTV Outpost GSC-0044 a member hauler deposited 1, then 18 fuel cells from its hold into the faction storage (the store read 0, 1, 19; 20:27 UTC).
- Test: scripts/tests/test_fleet_route_run.py, StoreFactionStepTests (two cases), both failed on the old runner first. game/routes/BLUEPRINT.md gains the row `store_faction`.
- The outpost for a route file: system gsc_0044, POI da9de8c360c46ffee15dee4e7d1b8476, base 443f0c5b2a1fbbcea95d13b76a797fe9; a stop there reads `"at": "gsc_0044:da9de8c360c46ffee15dee4e7d1b8476:443f0c5b2a1fbbcea95d13b76a797fe9"`; only a faction member docks.
